This directory is where scripts/stage-browser-app.sh puts the built browser
application, and where the Dockerfile copies it from. Its contents are build
output and are not committed — only this file is, so that `COPY web /app/web`
succeeds in a clean checkout where nothing has been staged.

An image built without staging serves no application. That is a supported
configuration: cde.web.app.path is unset by default, and a deployment that
serves the Angular build from its own web tier wants exactly that.
